Searched for an event technology service in Malaga? Locally that phrase covers a lot of ground, and not all of it is ground we stand on. Some Malaga production companies use "event technology" to mean live streaming, video mapping, LED walls and interactive touchscreens. That is not what Malaga Event Gear (MEG) offers, and we would rather tell you that up front than let you find out after a call.

What we do offer, under this same name, is the physical layer: RGBW and moving head event lighting, modular stage platforms sized to your room, and an on site technician who runs the equipment during your event. This page indexes that real layer, backed by experience going back to 1996, and closes with a direct list of what falls outside it.

## Brief Overview

---

Malaga Event Gear supplies the physical event technology layer for corporate events, conferences and celebrations across Malaga and the wider Costa del Sol: RGBW and moving head lighting, modular stage platforms, and dedicated on site technicians. It does not supply live streaming, video mapping, LED walls, interactive touchscreens or event management software, categories some local competitors market under the same "event technology" name.

This page cross links to our [audiovisual equipment rental service](/blog/audiovisual-equipment-rental-service/) pillar for the deeper lighting specs, our [AV technician hire](/blog/av-technician-hire/) guide for the on site technician role, and our [audio visual rental](/blog/audio-visual-rental/) pillar for the full package range. [Contact us](/contact/) to match a package to your event.

## Key Highlights

---

-   RGBW LED spotlights on the [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/), plus Beam/Spot moving head fixtures listed in our equipment catalog, for accent and stage lighting.

-   Modular stage platforms on the [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/), priced at 35 euros per square meter and sized to your room, not sold as a fixed truss unit.

-   A dedicated on site technician included on several of our packages: see our [AV technician hire](/blog/av-technician-hire/) guide for exactly which ones and how many hours.

-   A narrow, honest definition of "event technology" that excludes live streaming, video mapping, LED walls, interactive touchscreens and event management software, all covered plainly further down.

## Why "Event Technology" Means Something Different Here

Search "event technology service Malaga" and the results are a mix of local AV and production companies, not the software platforms the same phrase turns up internationally. Some of those local competitors run streaming, video mapping and interactive touchscreens as service lines. We looked at what a general search for that term turns up locally, and rather than stretch our catalog to match it, we are naming the gap directly.

MEG's version of event technology is physical, not digital: the lighting rig, the stage platform, and the technician standing next to the mixing console. If you are picturing a hybrid broadcast, a projection mapped facade, or an event app with RFID check in, this is the wrong page, and we would rather say so now than after you have described your event to us on the phone. If you are picturing a lit stage with a technician running the show, keep reading.

