## Stage Design and Setup

Stage design at MEG means one real, priced product: modular stage platforms on the [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/), an optional add on at 35 euros per square meter, sized to your room rather than sold as a fixed unit. It is a platform to raise speakers, a panel or a small band above floor level, not a scenic build.

We deployed exactly this for a two day corporate project with [Bmotion in Marbella](/blog/news-malaga-event-gear-delivers-premium-technical-support-for-bmotions-high-profile-corporate-project-in-marbella/), where modular platforms created the elevated presentation area the client needed for international guests.

![Modular stage platforms set up for a corporate presentation in Marbella.](https://cdn.malagaeventgear.com/blog/3076/2026.05.19-20-Bmotion-Marbella-3-1024x576.webp)

The modular staging deployed for the Bmotion Marbella project, alongside the gooseneck and wireless microphone systems that ran from the same platform.

We do not stock truss as a separate rental item, and we do not supply pipe and drape, backdrop hardware or scenic theatrical staging. If what you pictured was a themed stage set or a truss rig, see [What We Don't Offer](#what-we-dont-offer) below, and for the fuller staging breakdown alongside our lighting and screen inventory, see [Modular Staging for Corporate Events](/blog/audiovisual-equipment-rental-service/#modular-staging-for-corporate-events) on our audiovisual equipment rental service pillar.

## On Site Technical Support

A technician is part of several MEG packages, running the sound, lighting and screen for the duration of your event rather than leaving you to operate a rack of gear yourselves. We are not re answering the coverage details here: our [AV technician hire](/blog/av-technician-hire/) guide covers exactly which packages include a technician, how many hours each one covers, and what the role does and does not include on site.

## What We Don't Offer

A general search for event technology in Malaga turns up services from local production companies that are not part of our catalog. Here is the honest list, each claim already stated on a live page of ours:

-   **Live streaming or hybrid event streaming.** Our [audio visual rental for virtual events](/blog/audio-visual-rental-for-virtual-events/) guide states this directly: "We do not supply cameras, streaming encoders, or a recording service." You bring your own laptop, your conferencing software and your internet connection.

-   **Video mapping, LED walls or video walls.** Our [audiovisual equipment rental service](/blog/audiovisual-equipment-rental-service/) pillar is explicit: our large format display is a single 60 inch flat panel, not a modular tiled video wall, and our projector setups don't include facade projection or outdoor mapping.

-   **Interactive touchscreens or kiosks.** Our [audio visual rental for religious events](/blog/audio-visual-rental-for-religious-events/) guide rules this out on the same grounds it rules out an LED video wall: not part of our catalog.

-   **Interpretation, translation equipment or audience response/voting systems.** We do not stock this equipment ourselves, but we arrange it through a subcontracted partner for corporate and congress-grade events: [contact us](/contact/) with your requirements. See our [audiovisual equipment rental service](/blog/audiovisual-equipment-rental-service/#what-we-dont-offer) pillar for the same note.

-   **Event apps, RFID tracking or ticketing technology.** This sits outside our catalog, and it is a genuine scope boundary rather than a gap in the local market: the event technology competitors we researched for this page are physical AV and production companies too, not registration or ticketing platforms.

