## How Far in Advance to Book

Book as soon as your event date is confirmed. Demand on the Costa del Sol peaks during wedding season, from April through October, when technicians and lighting fixtures fill up first. Corporate bookings that need moving head lighting or modular staging should lock in the package early rather than wait for a final headcount, since both sit on our higher demand corporate packages.

## Conclusion

Event technology at Malaga Event Gear is a physical layer, not a digital one: RGBW and moving head lighting, modular stage platforms, and an on site technician running it all. It does not include streaming, video mapping, LED walls, interactive touchscreens or event management software, whatever a general search for the term might turn up locally. [Contact us](/contact/) to match a package to your event. For the full package range, see our [audio visual rental](/blog/audio-visual-rental/) pillar, and for the specialized equipment layer, see our [audiovisual equipment rental service](/blog/audiovisual-equipment-rental-service/) pillar.

## FAQs

### What Is "Event Technology" and What Does MEG Actually Provide?

At Malaga Event Gear, event technology means the physical layer of an event: RGBW and moving head lighting, modular stage platforms, and an on site technician. It does not mean streaming, video mapping or interactive software, which some local competitors market under the same name. See [Why "Event Technology" Means Something Different Here](#why-event-technology-means-something-different-here) above.

### Is Event Technology the Same as Audiovisual Equipment Rental?

They overlap but are not identical. Our [audio visual rental](/blog/audio-visual-rental/) pillar covers the full package range, from the [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/) up to the [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/), and our [audiovisual equipment rental service](/blog/audiovisual-equipment-rental-service/) pillar indexes the specialized equipment layer inside that catalog. This page is narrower still: it covers only the pieces of that catalog that fit an "event technology" framing, lighting, staging and on site support, and says plainly what falls outside it.

### Do You Provide Event Lighting Technology?

Yes. RGBW LED spotlights on the [Eco Pack](/packages/eco/), and Beam/Spot moving head fixtures for larger corporate stages, quoted on request. See [Event Lighting](#event-lighting) above.

### What Is Stage Design and Setup, and Do You Offer It?

We offer modular stage platforms on the [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/) at 35 euros per square meter, sized to your room. We do not offer scenic theatrical stage design, truss rigs, or pipe and drape. See [Stage Design and Setup](#stage-design-and-setup) above.

### Do You Provide On Site Technical Support?

Yes, on several packages. Our [AV technician hire](/blog/av-technician-hire/) guide covers exactly which packages include a technician and how many hours each one covers, rather than repeating that detail here.

### Do You Offer Live Streaming or Event Technology for Hybrid or Virtual Events?

No. Our [audio visual rental for virtual events](/blog/audio-visual-rental-for-virtual-events/) guide states it directly: we do not supply cameras, streaming encoders, or a recording service. You bring your own laptop, conferencing software and internet connection, and we supply the room's sound and screen.

### Do You Provide Video Mapping or LED and Video Walls?

No. Our large format display is a single 60 inch flat panel, not a modular tiled video wall, and our projector setups do not include facade projection or outdoor mapping. See [What We Don't Offer](#what-we-dont-offer) above.

### Do You Offer Interactive Touchscreens, Kiosks or Audience Response Technology?

Touchscreens and kiosks, no: our [audio visual rental for religious events](/blog/audio-visual-rental-for-religious-events/) guide rules those out on the same grounds it rules out a video wall. Audience response or voting systems, yes as an arranged service: we don't stock the hardware ourselves, so we bring in a subcontracted partner for corporate and congress-grade events.

### Do You Provide Event Apps, RFID Tracking or Ticketing Technology?

No. This is a scope boundary, not a gap we are hiding. It also sits outside what the local event technology competitors we looked at for this page actually sell, since they are physical AV and production companies rather than registration or ticketing platforms.

### How Far in Advance Should I Book Event Technology for My Event?

As early as your date is confirmed. Demand peaks during wedding season, from April through October, when technicians and moving head lighting fixtures are the first things to fill up. See [How Far in Advance to Book](#how-far-in-advance-to-book) above.
